ROOF_EXTRA = [
 ("What our SEO services for roofers <span class=\"ac\">include</span>",
  "<div class=\"grid\"><div class=\"card\"><h3>First month: the foundation</h3><p>A full check of your Google Business Profile against the searches in your service area, the right primary and secondary categories, every roofing service listed, your real service area, and your name, address and phone made to match on Google, Bing, Apple Maps, the BBB, Angi and Yelp.</p></div><div class=\"card\"><h3>Every month: steady proof</h3><p>Job photos and posts on your profile, a simple review link for happy homeowners, replies to reviews, one new or better service or town page, and a report of calls, direction requests and searches you can check in your own Google account.</p></div><div class=\"card\"><h3>Before storm season</h3><p>Storm damage, hail damage and insurance claim pages ready before the searches spike, plus profile posts that tell homeowners you are taking inspections. See <a href=\"/guides/roofing-leads-after-a-storm\">how roofers get more leads after a storm</a>.</p></div><div class=\"card\"><h3>Always: ChatGPT and AI answers</h3><p>Your company, towns and track record described the same way on your site and the directories AI assistants read, so they can name you when a homeowner asks who to call.</p></div></div>"),
 ("Local SEO or organic SEO: <span class=\"ac\">where roofers need to show up</span>",
  "<div class=\"grid\"><div class=\"card\"><h3>Local results: the map</h3><p>Searches like \"roofer near me\" and \"roof repair [town]\" show a map with three companies at the top. Google ranks these on relevance, distance and prominence, so your Google Business Profile, your reviews and how close you are to the searcher decide most of it.</p></div>"
  "<div class=\"card\"><h3>Organic results: the website</h3><p>Below the map are the regular results. Searches like \"how much does a new roof cost\" or \"does insurance cover hail damage\" often show no map at all. These depend on your website: a clear page for each service and town, honest answers to cost and insurance questions, and a site that loads fast on phones.</p></div>"
  "<div class=\"card\"><h3>Why a roofer needs both</h3><p>The map brings the ready-to-hire calls from nearby. The website wins the research searches and the towns at the edge of your service area, where you are too far away to make the map. Each one helps the other: your profile links to your pages, and your pages back up the services on your profile.</p></div></div>"),
 ("Google Maps for roofing companies: <span class=\"ac\">the part that brings calls</span>",
  "<p>Most roofers are service-area businesses: you go to the homeowner, they do not come to you. Google expects you to set the towns or ZIP codes you serve and hide an address customers cannot visit. Choose Roofing contractor as the primary category, list every roofing service in the homeowner's words, add job photos every month, and never add keywords to the business name, which can get a profile suspended. The step-by-step version is in our <a href=\"/guides/google-business-profile-for-roofers\">Google Business Profile optimization guide for roofers</a>, and if Google keeps asking you to verify, see <a href=\"/guides/google-business-profile-verification-problems\">verification problems and how to fix them</a>.</p>"),
 ("Storm season: <span class=\"ac\">why timing decides the work</span>",
  "<p>Searches for storm damage, hail damage and emergency tarping jump the days after a storm. Pages and profile changes take time to be found, so a roofing SEO agency should get your storm pages live and your profile ready months before your local hail, wind or hurricane season, not the week it hits. In winter, the work shifts to ice dams, leaks and inspections. See <a href=\"/guides/roofing-leads-after-a-storm\">the storm season playbook for roofers</a> and <a href=\"/guides/winter-roofing-leads\">how roofers get found in winter</a>.</p>"),
 ("What a roofing SEO agency <span class=\"ac\">costs</span>",
  "<p>Prices vary with how competitive your market is, how many towns you serve and how much needs fixing today. Ours are public: the first check is free, one-time fixes start at $120 for on-page work and $160 for technical work, and monthly local SEO for one location is $299 a month with no contract. For what drives the price and the red flags to watch for, read <a href=\"/guides/roofing-seo-cost\">how much roofing SEO costs</a>, and for survey averages across all trades, <a href=\"/guides/local-seo-cost\">how much local SEO costs per month</a>.</p>"),
 ("Hiring a local SEO agency for roofing companies: <span class=\"ac\">the first 90 days</span>",
  "<ol class=\"steps\"><li><b>Week 1: free check</b>We search like your customers do in your towns and send your rank on the map, the 3 companies above you and your top 3 fixes. No cost, no contract.</li><li><b>Weeks 2 to 4: profile and website fixes</b>Categories, services, service area, photos, tap-to-call and the estimate form. These are the changes that can help within weeks.</li><li><b>Months 2 and 3: pages and reviews</b>Service and town pages that answer what homeowners type, and a steady flow of reviews that name the job and the town. Rankings across a whole service area usually build over three to six months.</li></ol><p>Want to know the budget first? Read <a href=\"/guides/roofing-seo-cost\">how much roofing SEO costs</a> and <a href=\"/guides/roofing-seo-keywords\">the roofing keywords homeowners use</a>.</p>"),
 ("Your roofing website, <span class=\"ac\">kept in shape</span>",
  "<p>Your website is where a search becomes an inspection request. It needs your phone number and an estimate button at the top, a page for each service (repairs, replacements, storm damage, gutters, commercial), real job photos, and proof: licenses, insurance, warranties and reviews. It also needs looking after. Broken pages, a slow load on phones and an expired security certificate quietly cost you rankings. Our monthly plan covers this website maintenance along with the SEO.</p>"),
 ("Local Services Ads or SEO: <span class=\"ac\">which first?</span>",
  "<p>Google Local Services Ads put a Google Screened or Google Guaranteed badge above everything else, and you pay per lead. SEO brings the free calls from the map and the regular results, and keeps working when you stop paying. Most roofing companies do best with both. A strong Google Business Profile and steady reviews help your ads and your free rankings at the same time.</p>"),
 ("Choosing a roofing SEO company: <span class=\"ac\">5 questions to ask</span>",
  "<ol class=\"steps\"><li><b>Will I see every change?</b>A good roofing SEO company shows you what it changes on your profile and website, before and after.</li><li><b>Can I check results myself?</b>You should see calls, direction requests and searches in your own Google Business Profile and Search Console, not only in their report.</li><li><b>Do you promise #1?</b>Walk away if they do. Google says no one can guarantee a ranking.</li><li><b>Do I own everything?</b>Your profile, website, pages and reviews should stay yours if you leave.</li><li><b>What happens in storm season?</b>Ask how they prepare your pages and profile before the storms, not after.</li></ol>"),
]

